From 065d5cabec624645a6869f9efda68d6389f47eb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:15:21 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Cheats: none run while the game has ad hoc play running

A cheat changes one player's game only. In a network battle the two
games then part (the port's battle cheats write "your" fighter, a
different fighter on each player's game, so even the same cheats on both
part them), and the other player fights against the cheat. So while the
game has ad hoc play running (adhoc_networking_on(): from its
sceNetAdhocctlInit or sceNetAdhocInit to the Term), no cheat runs, the
port's own or the file's. Nothing in the settings changes: the cheats
that were on run again once the game leaves ad hoc play.

- cheats: paused_online(), asked before each pass; the log says when the
  cheats pause and run again. <prefix>_CHEATS_ONLINE=1 runs them all the
  same (the old behaviour).
- ui/menu: the Cheats page says so while they are paused.
- PROFILE_GUIDE: a port's own cheat run from a hook asks paused_online()
  too.

Tested on Windows (clang) with Dissidia 012, two copies through a
loopback server: one copy with Bravery 9,999 and Infinite HP on ran them
until it entered the Online Lobby, then not at all through a battle (the
HUD kept the battle's own Bravery); back at the Start Menu they ran
again, and paused again in the lobby, the Cheats page showing the line.
Not tested: Linux, the Steam Deck, Android, another game, Group Battle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
